# fx outline on a brushed fill follows the coverage its brush leaves, 192x72, three 48px squares
# on paper at y 36, each with an outline in its fill's line color: dark brown on gold, dark blue
# on blue.
# Cell 1 (x 32), gold square with chip and outline 3: the edge is bitten by flakes, and the
# ring follows every bite inward, so paper shows inside each bite with the ring around it. No bite
# shows solid ring color across it and the ring never runs straight along the square's geometry.
# Cell 2 (x 96), blue square with dry and outline 2: horizontal streaks break the blue, and the
# ring runs into each streak from both sides. Every streak is narrower than the ring, so each
# one fills with dark blue and no paper shows inside the square. The square's own edge stays
# straight with a few small notches where a streak reaches it.
# Cell 3 (x 160), gold square with no brush and outline 3: a plain square ring with round corners
# around solid gold, as before.
# The .svg target uses profile:svg: an outline that traces a brushed fill bakes with its node into
# a raster tile, so cells 1 and 2 look like the PNG's, and cell 3 stays a path and an outline path.
@artboard 192x72
@target brush/outline.png
@target brush/outline.svg profile:svg

use std/brushes { dry chip }

rect 48 at:32,36 fill:p.gold.2 brush:chip(strength:.9 scale:2) name:chipped
  fx outline 3
rect 48 at:96,36 fill:p.blue.2 brush:dry(strength:.6) name:streaked
  fx outline 2
rect 48 at:160,36 fill:p.gold.2 name:plain
  fx outline 3
